# The Target's compose environment. Seeded on the Target by whatever installed
# the stack — the deploy script today, the creator CLI once it lands — filling
# in what can be read off the Target itself. Never committed, and never copied
# back to the operator's machine.
#
# Read by compose, which passes what the Harness needs into its container, and
# by the Onboarding commands, which still run on the Target and take their
# answer to "where do Projects live" from here.

# Directory on the Target holding the Project checkouts. Mounted into the
# Harness at the same path, so a Sandbox's bind mounts resolve on the Target.
# Auto-filled from ~/.claude-tmux/.env when present.
WORKSPACE_ROOT=

# The operator on the Target who owns those checkouts, and the Target's docker
# group. The Harness runs as that user and joins that group, so worktrees are
# owned correctly and the mounted socket is usable. Auto-filled.
OPERATOR_UID=
OPERATOR_GID=
DOCKER_GID=

# The harness holds no agent credentials: each Project keeps its own token in
# its .sandcastle/.env, which sandcastle reads natively. Onboard a checkout
# with `init-project <name>` and rotate tokens with `sync-env`.

# Inngest server credentials. Auto-generated (openssl rand -hex 32) on the
# Target when left empty.
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=

# Optional overrides.
#AGENT_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# The Dispatch port, published on Target loopback only. Nothing authenticates
# behind it — do not publish it anywhere else without putting auth in front.
#PORT=3000
